{"title":"Career roadmap · Government Affairs Executive","role":"Government Affairs Executive","summary":"A Government Affairs Executive helps an organisation understand, monitor and engage with the government and public-policy environment. The role can involve policy tracking, regulatory research, stakeholder engagement, government communications, consultation responses, public affairs, compliance coordination and policy analysis.","facts":{"Starts":"Year 1 UG · 2026","Current degree":"BBA / BMS / BBM – Public Policy / Political Management"},"about":[{"label":"Primary skills","text":"Policy research, regulatory monitoring, stakeholder management, business understanding, communication and analytical thinking"},{"label":"Important distinction","text":"Government Affairs is different from becoming a civil servant or elected politician"}],"intro":[],"horizons":[{"period":"2026–2030","question":"What can I enter now?","output":"Build policy, economics, business, governance and communication foundations"},{"period":"2030–2035","question":"How should I specialise?","output":"Work as Government Affairs Executive/Analyst and develop industry expertise"},{"period":"2035–2040","question":"How should I evolve?","output":"Manage regulatory relationships, policy strategy and major stakeholder programmes"},{"period":"2040–2046","question":"How can I remain relevant?","output":"Progress toward Government Affairs Director, Public Affairs Lead, Policy Strategy or senior regulatory leadership"}],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"For a student pursuing BBA – Public Policy / Political Management, this is a strong and relevant career pathway. However, Government Affairs is broader than political work: the role may exist in corporates, industry associations, consulting firms, public-policy organisations, NGOs, think tanks and regulated sectors."},{"type":"p","text":"A typical progression can be:"},{"type":"flow","items":["BBA","Public Policy/Government Affairs Internship","Government Affairs Executive / Public Affairs Analyst","Senior Executive/Manager","Government Affairs Manager","Director/Public Affairs Lead"]}]},{"heading":"Career-route check","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Strong/direct alignment."},{"type":"p","text":"BBA Public Policy/Political Management provides a useful combination of business, policy and political-system knowledge."},{"type":"p","text":"To become employable in Government Affairs, the student should additionally build:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Public-policy research"},{"text":"Regulatory analysis"},{"text":"Government processes"},{"text":"Legislative tracking"},{"text":"Business impact assessment"},{"text":"Stakeholder mapping"},{"text":"Policy writing"},{"text":"Data analysis"},{"text":"Professional communication"},{"text":"Industry-specific regulatory knowledge"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Timeline assumption"},{"type":"p","text":"This roadmap assumes a 4-year undergraduate programme beginning in 2026 and graduating around 2030."}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["When","Build this","Learn from","Proof of progress","Gap it moves"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 1"},{"text":"Business, economics, communication and government basics"},{"text":"College + NPTEL"},{"text":"Policy/business assignment"},{"text":"Foundation"}],[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 2"},{"text":"Indian Constitution, governance and public institutions"},{"text":"Official government resources"},{"text":"Government-system report"},{"text":"Governance"}],[{"text":"Year 2 Sem 1"},{"text":"Public policy, political economy and regulatory systems"},{"text":"Policy courses + reports"},{"text":"Policy brief"},{"text":"Policy knowledge"}],[{"text":"Year 2 Sem 2"},{"text":"Data analysis, research methods and stakeholder mapping"},{"text":"Excel/analytics + policy research"},{"text":"Data-backed policy brief"},{"text":"Analytical capability"}],[{"text":"Year 3 Sem 1"},{"text":"Legislative/regulatory tracking, industry policy and impact analysis"},{"text":"Government notifications + industry reports"},{"text":"Regulatory-impact case"},{"text":"Government affairs"}],[{"text":"Year 3 Sem 2"},{"text":"Government affairs/public policy internship"},{"text":"Think tank/company/association"},{"text":"Internship portfolio"},{"text":"Professional readiness"}],[{"text":"Year 4 Sem 1"},{"text":"Negotiation, advocacy ethics, public affairs and sector specialisation"},{"text":"Industry + policy resources"},{"text":"Government-affairs strategy case"},{"text":"Strategic capability"}],[{"text":"Year 4 Sem 2"},{"text":"Placement, interviews, policy portfolio and competitive-exam awareness"},{"text":"Job descriptions + mock interviews"},{"text":"Resume + 3–5 policy cases"},{"text":"Employability"}]]},{"type":"p","text":"Useful academic resources include NPTEL.","url":"https://nptel.ac.in/"},{"type":"p","text":"For primary government information, prioritise official government and parliamentary sources rather than relying on social-media summaries."},{"type":"h","text":"Core Government Affairs skill stack"},{"type":"h","text":"1. Indian government structure"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Union Government"},{"text":"State Governments"},{"text":"Local government"},{"text":"Parliament"},{"text":"State legislatures"},{"text":"Ministries"},{"text":"Departments"},{"text":"Regulators"},{"text":"Constitutional bodies"},{"text":"Statutory bodies"},{"text":"Public-sector organisations"},{"text":"Local authorities"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand the difference between:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Policy","Law","Rule","Regulation","Notification","Implementation"]}]},{"heading":"Public policy","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn the policy cycle:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Problem identification","Research","Policy formulation","Consultation","Decision","Implementation","Monitoring","Evaluation"]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Policy objectives"},{"text":"Stakeholders"},{"text":"Evidence"},{"text":"Alternatives"},{"text":"Costs"},{"text":"Benefits"},{"text":"Trade-offs"},{"text":"Implementation risks"},{"text":"Policy outcomes"}]}]},{"heading":"Regulatory affairs","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn how regulations affect businesses."},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Regulatory notifications"},{"text":"Compliance requirements"},{"text":"Licensing"},{"text":"Reporting"},{"text":"Industry standards"},{"text":"Regulatory consultations"},{"text":"Government circulars"},{"text":"Policy changes"},{"text":"Regulatory impact"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A Government Affairs Executive should be able to answer:"},{"type":"p","text":"What changed, which organisation/business unit is affected, when does it apply, what action is required, and what are the business implications?"}]},{"heading":"Legislative tracking","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Develop the ability to monitor:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Bills"},{"text":"Acts"},{"text":"Rules"},{"text":"Parliamentary questions"},{"text":"Committee reports"},{"text":"Government notifications"},{"text":"Consultations"},{"text":"Policy announcements"},{"text":"Regulatory developments"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Use primary sources wherever possible."},{"type":"p","text":"Useful official sources include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Digital Sansad","url":"https://sansad.in/"},{"text":"India Code","url":"https://www.indiacode.nic.in/"},{"text":"Press Information Bureau","url":"https://pib.gov.in/"}]}]},{"heading":"Policy research","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Master:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Literature review"},{"text":"Desk research"},{"text":"Primary research"},{"text":"Secondary research"},{"text":"Interviews"},{"text":"Surveys"},{"text":"Stakeholder analysis"},{"text":"Comparative policy analysis"},{"text":"Evidence evaluation"},{"text":"Policy recommendations"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Learn to distinguish:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Fact","Interpretation","Assumption","Recommendation"]},{"type":"p","text":"This is particularly important in policy work."}]},{"heading":"Policy brief writing","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A good policy brief should clearly communicate:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Issue"},{"text":"Context"},{"text":"Evidence"},{"text":"Stakeholders"},{"text":"Existing policy"},{"text":"Problem/gap"},{"text":"Policy options"},{"text":"Advantages/disadvantages"},{"text":"Recommendation"},{"text":"Implementation considerations"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The student should practise producing 2–4 page policy briefs."}]},{"heading":"Business and economic analysis","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Government Affairs sits at the intersection of policy and business."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Microeconomics"},{"text":"Macroeconomics"},{"text":"Inflation"},{"text":"Interest rates"},{"text":"Employment"},{"text":"Taxation"},{"text":"Trade"},{"text":"Industrial policy"},{"text":"Competition"},{"text":"Investment"},{"text":"Public expenditure"},{"text":"Sector economics"},{"text":"Cost-benefit analysis"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The student should understand:"},{"type":"p","text":"How does a policy change affect customers, companies, employees, investors and government objectives?"}]},{"heading":"Stakeholder mapping","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn to identify:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Central ministries"},{"text":"State departments"},{"text":"Regulators"},{"text":"MPs/MLAs where professionally relevant"},{"text":"Industry associations"},{"text":"Companies"},{"text":"NGOs"},{"text":"Think tanks"},{"text":"Researchers"},{"text":"Consumer groups"},{"text":"Local authorities"},{"text":"Professional bodies"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Create stakeholder maps based on:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Interest","Influence","Impact","Position"],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"Government engagement","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn professional approaches to:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Meetings"},{"text":"Consultation submissions"},{"text":"Industry representations"},{"text":"Policy roundtables"},{"text":"Conferences"},{"text":"Government correspondence"},{"text":"Regulatory consultations"},{"text":"Industry-association engagement"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The emphasis should always be on lawful, transparent and ethical engagement."},{"type":"p","text":"Government Affairs should never be treated as a shortcut for improper influence or preferential access."}]},{"heading":"Industry specialisation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Government Affairs professionals become significantly more valuable when they understand a particular sector."},{"type":"p","text":"Possible specialisations:"},{"type":"h","text":"Technology"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AI"},{"text":"Data protection"},{"text":"Digital regulation"},{"text":"Cybersecurity"},{"text":"Telecom"},{"text":"Platforms"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Finance"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Banking"},{"text":"Insurance"},{"text":"FinTech"},{"text":"Capital markets"},{"text":"Financial regulation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Healthcare"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Pharmaceuticals"},{"text":"Medical devices"},{"text":"HealthTech"},{"text":"Healthcare regulation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Energy"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Renewable energy"},{"text":"Electricity"},{"text":"Oil & gas"},{"text":"Energy transition"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Agriculture"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AgriTech"},{"text":"Food policy"},{"text":"Agricultural markets"},{"text":"Rural development"}]},{"type":"h","text":"E-commerce"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Consumer protection"},{"text":"Competition"},{"text":"Digital commerce"},{"text":"Data/privacy"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Infrastructure"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Transport"},{"text":"Roads"},{"text":"Ports"},{"text":"Urban development"}]}]},{"heading":"Data and analytics","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Government Affairs increasingly requires evidence-based analysis."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"h","text":"Excel"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"XLOOKUP"},{"text":"SUMIFS"},{"text":"COUNTIFS"},{"text":"Pivot tables"},{"text":"Charts"},{"text":"Power Query"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Power BI"},{"type":"p","text":"Build dashboards for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Regulatory changes"},{"text":"Sector indicators"},{"text":"Government schemes"},{"text":"Policy KPIs"},{"text":"Economic indicators"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Basic SQL"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"SELECT"},{"text":"WHERE"},{"text":"GROUP BY"},{"text":"JOIN"},{"text":"CASE"},{"text":"Aggregations"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Practice with SQLBolt.","url":"https://sqlbolt.com/"}]},{"heading":"Communication","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Develop excellent:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Policy writing"},{"text":"Business writing"},{"text":"Presentation"},{"text":"Public speaking"},{"text":"Briefing-note writing"},{"text":"Executive summaries"},{"text":"Meeting notes"},{"text":"Email communication"},{"text":"Negotiation"},{"text":"Stakeholder communication"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The ability to explain a complex regulation in one page for a senior executive is a valuable Government Affairs skill."}]},{"heading":"AI for Government Affairs","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Use AI responsibly for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Policy-document summarisation"},{"text":"Regulatory change monitoring"},{"text":"Document comparison"},{"text":"Research assistance"},{"text":"Stakeholder mapping"},{"text":"Data analysis"},{"text":"Drafting first versions of policy briefs"},{"text":"Scenario analysis"}]},{"type":"p","text":"But verify every important factual or legal claim against the original government/regulator source."},{"type":"p","text":"AI-generated policy summaries should never be treated as the legal text itself."},{"type":"h","text":"Portfolio projects"},{"type":"h","text":"Project 1 — Policy brief"},{"type":"p","text":"Choose a current issue such as:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AI regulation"},{"text":"Digital payments"},{"text":"Electric vehicles"},{"text":"Renewable energy"},{"text":"Data protection"},{"text":"E-commerce"},{"text":"Agricultural reforms"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Create a 3–5 page policy brief with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Problem"},{"text":"Evidence"},{"text":"Stakeholders"},{"text":"Existing policy"},{"text":"Policy alternatives"},{"text":"Recommendation"},{"text":"Implementation considerations"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 2 — Regulatory tracker"},{"type":"p","text":"Build an Excel/Power BI tracker with:"},{"type":"table","header":["Field","Example"],"rows":[[{"text":"Regulation"},{"text":"New rule/notification"}],[{"text":"Authority"},{"text":"Regulator/ministry"}],[{"text":"Date"},{"text":"Publication date"}],[{"text":"Sector"},{"text":"Technology"}],[{"text":"Impact"},{"text":"High/Medium/Low"}],[{"text":"Business unit"},{"text":"Product/operations"}],[{"text":"Action"},{"text":"Required response"}],[{"text":"Deadline"},{"text":"Applicable date"}],[{"text":"Status"},{"text":"Open/closed"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 3 — Industry policy map"},{"type":"p","text":"Choose an industry such as AI, FinTech, healthcare or energy."},{"type":"p","text":"Map:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Relevant ministries"},{"text":"Regulators"},{"text":"Major laws"},{"text":"Key policies"},{"text":"Industry associations"},{"text":"Major stakeholders"},{"text":"Current policy issues"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 4 — Government affairs case"},{"type":"p","text":"Analyse a hypothetical policy change."},{"type":"p","text":"Answer:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"What changed?"},{"text":"Why did government introduce it?"},{"text":"Who is affected?"},{"text":"What is the business impact?"},{"text":"What compliance action is required?"},{"text":"What are the implementation risks?"},{"text":"What stakeholder engagement may be appropriate?"},{"text":"What should the company communicate internally?"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 5 — Policy impact dashboard"},{"type":"p","text":"Build a Power BI dashboard covering:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Economic indicators"},{"text":"Sector growth"},{"text":"Government spending"},{"text":"Regulatory events"},{"text":"Policy announcements"},{"text":"Industry metrics"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Use Microsoft Power BI.","url":"https://www.microsoft.com/power-platform/products/power-bi"},{"type":"h","text":"Four-year honours / extended-degree variant"},{"type":"p","text":"If the student follows a 4-year honours/research pathway, use the additional depth for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Public-policy research"},{"text":"Political economy"},{"text":"Regulatory economics"},{"text":"Public administration"},{"text":"Impact evaluation"},{"text":"Quantitative policy analysis"},{"text":"Government data analysis"},{"text":"Legislative research"},{"text":"Policy implementation"},{"text":"A substantial policy research project"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A strong research project could examine:"},{"type":"h","text":"“Business and economic impacts of emerging AI regulation in India.”"},{"type":"h","text":"Government Affairs specialisation lanes"},{"type":"table","header":["Lane","Core stack","Senior role it leads to"],"rows":[[{"text":"Corporate Government Affairs"},{"text":"Business + policy + stakeholder management"},{"text":"Government Affairs Manager"}],[{"text":"Regulatory Affairs"},{"text":"Regulation + compliance + policy"},{"text":"Regulatory Affairs Manager"}],[{"text":"Technology Policy"},{"text":"Technology + AI + digital regulation"},{"text":"Technology Policy Lead"}],[{"text":"Financial Policy"},{"text":"Banking + finance + regulation"},{"text":"Financial Policy Lead"}],[{"text":"Healthcare Policy"},{"text":"Healthcare + regulation + policy"},{"text":"Healthcare Government Affairs Lead"}],[{"text":"Energy Policy"},{"text":"Energy + economics + regulation"},{"text":"Energy Policy Director"}],[{"text":"Trade Policy"},{"text":"Economics + trade + government"},{"text":"Trade Policy Manager"}],[{"text":"Public Affairs"},{"text":"Communication + policy + stakeholder engagement"},{"text":"Public Affairs Director"}],[{"text":"Policy Consulting"},{"text":"Research + strategy + policy"},{"text":"Policy Consultant / Principal"}],[{"text":"Think Tank Research"},{"text":"Research + economics + policy"},{"text":"Senior Policy Researcher"}],[{"text":"Industry Association"},{"text":"Sector knowledge + advocacy + policy"},{"text":"Policy/Advocacy Director"}],[{"text":"ESG/Public Policy"},{"text":"Sustainability + regulation + business"},{"text":"ESG/Public Policy Lead"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Evolve and stay relevant · 2035–2046"},{"type":"p","text":"Government Affairs is moving toward evidence-based policy intelligence."},{"type":"p","text":"The future professional should be able to combine:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Regulatory monitoring"},{"text":"Policy research"},{"text":"Business strategy"},{"text":"Economic analysis"},{"text":"Data analytics"},{"text":"AI-assisted research"},{"text":"Stakeholder management"},{"text":"Scenario planning"},{"text":"Public communication"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The career should evolve from:"},{"type":"h","text":"“I track government announcements.”"},{"type":"p","text":"to:"},{"type":"p","text":"“I understand policy developments, quantify their business impact and help the organisation respond responsibly.”"}]},{"heading":"Internships","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Government, policy and public-sector exposure"},{"type":"table","header":["Organisation / route","Possible exposure"],"rows":[[{"text":"NITI Aayog","url":"https://www.niti.gov.in/"},{"text":"Policy research and development strategy"}],[{"text":"Ministry of Commerce & Industry","url":"https://www.commerce.gov.in/"},{"text":"Trade and industry policy"}],[{"text":"Ministry of Electronics & Information Technology","url":"https://www.meity.gov.in/"},{"text":"Digital and technology policy"}],[{"text":"Ministry of Corporate Affairs","url":"https://www.mca.gov.in/"},{"text":"Corporate regulation and policy"}],[{"text":"SEBI","url":"https://www.sebi.gov.in/"},{"text":"Financial regulation"}],[{"text":"RBI","url":"https://www.rbi.org.in/"},{"text":"Banking, monetary and financial policy"}],[{"text":"Competition Commission of India","url":"https://www.cci.gov.in/"},{"text":"Competition policy"}],[{"text":"Press Information Bureau","url":"https://pib.gov.in/"},{"text":"Government communication"}],[{"text":"PM Internship Scheme","url":"https://pminternship.mca.gov.in/"},{"text":"Industry exposure where eligible"}],[{"text":"Parliament/research programmes"},{"text":"Legislative and policy research"}]]},{"type":"p","text":"Internship availability and eligibility change by organisation and year."},{"type":"h","text":"Private-sector internships"},{"type":"p","text":"Target:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Government Affairs Intern"},{"text":"Public Policy Intern"},{"text":"Regulatory Affairs Intern"},{"text":"Public Affairs Intern"},{"text":"Policy Research Intern"},{"text":"Corporate Affairs Intern"},{"text":"ESG/Public Policy Intern"},{"text":"Government Relations Intern"},{"text":"Industry Association Intern"},{"text":"Political/Public Policy Research Intern"},{"text":"Strategy Intern"},{"text":"Regulatory Intelligence Intern"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Target employers such as:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Technology companies"},{"text":"FinTech companies"},{"text":"Banks"},{"text":"Healthcare/pharma"},{"text":"Energy companies"},{"text":"Telecom"},{"text":"E-commerce"},{"text":"Automotive"},{"text":"Infrastructure"},{"text":"Consulting firms"},{"text":"Industry associations"},{"text":"Think tanks"},{"text":"NGOs"},{"text":"Public-policy organisations"}]}]},{"heading":"Certifications in demand","kind":"certifications","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Certification / learning route","Why it helps"],"rows":[[{"text":"NPTEL Public Policy / Economics / Management"},{"text":"Academic foundation"}],[{"text":"Public Policy certification"},{"text":"Policy concepts"}],[{"text":"Regulatory affairs training"},{"text":"Regulatory understanding"}],[{"text":"Political economy"},{"text":"Policy-business relationship"}],[{"text":"Economics"},{"text":"Policy analysis"}],[{"text":"Research methodology"},{"text":"Evidence-based research"}],[{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Policy/business analysis"}],[{"text":"Power BI"},{"text":"Policy dashboards"}],[{"text":"SQL"},{"text":"Data analysis"}],[{"text":"Project management"},{"text":"Programme execution"}],[{"text":"Negotiation"},{"text":"Stakeholder management"}],[{"text":"AI for policy/research"},{"text":"Modern research capability"}]]},{"type":"p","text":"For Government Affairs, demonstrated policy research and writing ability is generally more valuable than accumulating unrelated certificates."}]},{"heading":"Careers you can be hired as","kind":"careers","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Role","Stack the posting asks for","Where the student proves it"],"rows":[[{"text":"Government Affairs Executive"},{"text":"Policy + government relations"},{"text":"Policy portfolio"}],[{"text":"Government Relations Executive"},{"text":"Stakeholder + government knowledge"},{"text":"Internship"}],[{"text":"Public Policy Analyst"},{"text":"Research + economics + policy"},{"text":"Policy briefs"}],[{"text":"Regulatory Affairs Executive"},{"text":"Regulation + compliance"},{"text":"Regulatory tracker"}],[{"text":"Public Affairs Executive"},{"text":"Communication + policy"},{"text":"Public-affairs project"}],[{"text":"Corporate Affairs Executive"},{"text":"Business + government relations"},{"text":"Corporate-policy case"}],[{"text":"Policy Research Associate"},{"text":"Research + writing"},{"text":"Research portfolio"}],[{"text":"Regulatory Analyst"},{"text":"Regulation + data"},{"text":"Regulatory-impact analysis"}],[{"text":"Government Relations Analyst"},{"text":"Stakeholder research + policy"},{"text":"Stakeholder map"}],[{"text":"Policy Consultant Trainee"},{"text":"Research + strategy"},{"text":"Consulting case"}],[{"text":"ESG/Public Policy Associate"},{"text":"Sustainability + regulation"},{"text":"ESG policy project"}],[{"text":"Industry Association Executive"},{"text":"Sector + policy + advocacy"},{"text":"Industry research"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Career reality"},{"type":"p","text":"Government Affairs Executive is generally a private-sector/corporate/public-affairs role, while government employment follows a separate recruitment structure."},{"type":"p","text":"A BBA graduate should not assume:"},{"type":"flow","items":["BBA","Government Affairs Executive","Government Officer"]},{"type":"p","text":"These are different career systems."},{"type":"p","text":"For a government career, the student may instead need to pursue the relevant UPSC/state PSC/recruitment examination or department-specific recruitment route, depending on the intended post."}]},{"heading":"Postgraduate study in India","kind":"pg_india","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["PG route","Best suited for"],"rows":[[{"text":"MBA Public Policy"},{"text":"Corporate/public-policy leadership"}],[{"text":"MBA Government / Public Affairs"},{"text":"Government relations"}],[{"text":"Master of Public Policy (MPP)"},{"text":"Policy analysis"}],[{"text":"Master of Public Administration (MPA)"},{"text":"Public administration"}],[{"text":"MA Political Science"},{"text":"Political/governance pathway"}],[{"text":"MA Economics"},{"text":"Economic policy"}],[{"text":"M.Sc Public Policy / Policy Analytics"},{"text":"Quantitative policy"}],[{"text":"MBA Strategy"},{"text":"Corporate strategy + policy"}],[{"text":"MBA International Business"},{"text":"Trade and global policy"}],[{"text":"LLM / regulatory law pathway"},{"text":"Legal/regulatory specialisation where eligible"}],[{"text":"PG Diploma in Public Policy"},{"text":"Targeted policy specialisation"}],[{"text":"PhD in Public Policy"},{"text":"Research and academia"}]]},{"type":"p","text":"Potential research funding may include institution-specific fellowships and broader programmes such as PMRF where the student meets the applicable eligibility conditions.","url":"https://www.pmrf.in/"}]},{"heading":"Study abroad, country by country","kind":"abroad","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Country","Example universities / ecosystem","Scholarship route","Gate to check"],"rows":[[{"text":"USA"},{"text":"Harvard Kennedy School, Georgetown, Duke, University of Chicago"},{"text":"University funding / Fulbright where eligible"},{"text":"Programme prerequisites"}],[{"text":"UK"},{"text":"LSE, Oxford, Cambridge, UCL, King's College London"},{"text":"University scholarships / Chevening where eligible"},{"text":"Programme requirements"}],[{"text":"Germany"},{"text":"Hertie School, relevant public-policy programmes"},{"text":"DAAD"},{"text":"Programme prerequisites"}],[{"text":"Canada"},{"text":"University of Toronto, McGill, UBC"},{"text":"University funding"},{"text":"Programme requirements"}],[{"text":"Australia"},{"text":"ANU, University of Melbourne, UNSW"},{"text":"University scholarships / Australia Awards where eligible"},{"text":"Programme and visa"}],[{"text":"Singapore"},{"text":"NUS, NTU, SMU"},{"text":"University scholarships"},{"text":"Highly competitive admissions"}],[{"text":"Netherlands"},{"text":"Leiden, Erasmus University Rotterdam, University of Amsterdam"},{"text":"University scholarships"},{"text":"Programme prerequisites"}]]},{"type":"p","text":"Useful official scholarship resources include DAAD India and USIEF.","url":"https://www.daad.in/en/"},{"type":"h","text":"Application pack"},{"type":"p","text":"Prepare:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Academic transcripts"},{"text":"CV"},{"text":"Statement of Purpose"},{"text":"Recommendation letters"},{"text":"English-language test where required"},{"text":"Policy briefs"},{"text":"Research project"},{"text":"Internship experience"},{"text":"Data-analysis work"},{"text":"Leadership/community experience"},{"text":"Financial documents"},{"text":"Passport and visa documentation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A portfolio of well-researched policy briefs can be particularly valuable for this pathway."}]},{"heading":"Going forward","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Corporate Government Affairs progression"},{"type":"flow","items":["BBA – Public Policy / Political Management","Government Affairs / Public Policy Internship","Government Affairs Executive / Policy Analyst","Senior Government Affairs Executive / Policy Manager","Government Affairs Manager","Senior Manager / Public Affairs Lead","Director – Government Affairs / Public Policy","VP Government Affairs / Corporate Affairs / Public Policy"]},{"type":"h","text":"Alternative policy route"},{"type":"flow","items":["BBA","Policy Research Intern","Research Associate / Policy Analyst","Senior Policy Analyst","Policy Consultant / Principal","Policy Director"]},{"type":"h","text":"Government-service alternative"},{"type":"p","text":"If the student's actual ambition is government employment rather than corporate Government Affairs, consider a separate preparation track:"},{"type":"flow","items":["BBA","UPSC / State PSC / department-specific recruitment","Government administrative/policy role"]},{"type":"p","text":"The exact examination and qualification requirements depend on the intended service/post and the relevant recruitment notification."},{"type":"h","text":"PhD routes"},{"type":"p","text":"Potential research areas:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Public policy"},{"text":"Political economy"},{"text":"Public administration"},{"text":"Regulatory economics"},{"text":"Technology policy"},{"text":"AI governance"},{"text":"Digital policy"},{"text":"International trade"},{"text":"Development economics"},{"text":"Healthcare policy"},{"text":"Energy policy"},{"text":"Environmental policy"},{"text":"Competition policy"},{"text":"Public finance"},{"text":"Governance and institutions"}]},{"type":"note","label":"2040–2046","text":"Long-term evolution"},{"type":"p","text":"Senior Government Affairs professionals should move beyond monitoring policies and become strategic policy advisors to business leadership."},{"type":"p","text":"Potential destinations include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Government Affairs Director"},{"text":"Public Policy Director"},{"text":"Regulatory Affairs Director"},{"text":"Public Affairs Director"},{"text":"Corporate Affairs Head"},{"text":"Policy Strategy Head"},{"text":"Government Relations Head"},{"text":"Chief Corporate Affairs Officer"},{"text":"Senior Policy Consultant"},{"text":"Think Tank Director"},{"text":"Public-policy entrepreneur"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The strongest long-term profile will combine:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Public Policy","Business Strategy","Economics","Regulation","Data","Stakeholder Management","Technology","Ethical Leadership"],"sep":"+"}]}]}